Gitea 28.2.0 with ACCOUNT_LINKING=auto links an OAuth2 sign-in whose account
creation collides with an existing user first by name and then by primary email
(createUserInContext in routers/web/auth/auth.go). The email step hands any
account to whoever holds its address at the identity provider, and the OIDC
callback is the one Gitea path oauth2-proxy does not gate.

The email step is removed: a collision links only to the individual user whose
name equals the preferred_username of the sign-in, which Keycloak does not let a
user change (editUsernameAllowed false). Any other collision is refused with
Gitea's own "email already used" or "username taken" message on the sign-in
page.

Generated with `diff -u` against the gitea-src-28.2.0 tarball and applied with
`git apply`, which allows no fuzz, so the build fails instead of landing a hunk
somewhere upstream moved it to.

